        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: restore terminal pgrp after PATH lookup",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Preserve terminal foreground ownership across interactive PATH probes so `watch` sessions and Ctrl+C remain responsive.\n- Serialize only probes with a controlling terminal, using a close-on-exec `/dev/tty` descriptor so redirected stdin cannot bypass recovery.\n- Restore only when the exact spawned probe process group still owns the foreground, preserving unrelated newer jobs.\n- Verify process-group setup and guard `tcsetpgrp` with a temporary thread-local `SIGTTOU` mask.\n\n## Validation\n- Exact head: `804d614a3f77d8bc6125b824e8cc9a274ae7da84`.\n- Focused path/foreground suites: 51/51 passed.\n- `make check`: SwiftFormat and SwiftLint clean.\n- Zero-retry full suite: 613/613 selections, 52/52 groups first-pass green, no retries, recoveries, or timeouts.\n- Autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Real controlling-PTY proof through public `ShellCommandLocator.commandV`: two concurrent interactive zsh probes resolved successfully with worker stdin redirected to `/dev/null`; the original foreground group was restored and a literal Ctrl+C byte reached the foreground sentinel.\n- Developer ID-signed debug bundle from exact head passed strict code-sign and Gatekeeper verification; bundled CLI reports CodexBar 0.42.1.\n- Production CodexBar PID, executable path, and start time remained unchanged.\n\n## Risk\nThe change is limited to shell PATH probing when a controlling terminal exists. Non-terminal app and CI probes retain the concurrent fast path, and restoration fails closed if terminal ownership changes to any group other than the exact probe.\n\n## Dependencies\nNo dependency changes; freshness review not applicable.\n",
